            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0707" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/6499: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-19T15:00:00-06:00">December 19, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:33 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>382. My 377, December 14, 1 p.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d673-f1"/> General Tapia,
                    Chief of the President’s Military Staff, tells me that according to his
                    information <pb facs="0708" n="590" xml:id="pg590"/> Sandino is endeavoring to
                    purchase a farm near Merida on which to live and that he finds difficulty in
                    securing the purchase money. General Tapia says he has no information whatever
                    that would indicate Sandino is planning to return to Nicaragua.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nicaragua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
